  "wikitext": "{{Short description|Species of flowering plant}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| genus = Ipomoea\n| species = pedicellaris\n| authority = [[George Bentham|Benth.]]<ref name=POWO/>\n}}\n\n'''''Ipomoea pedicellaris''''' is a species of climbing herbaceous plant. It belongs to the morning glory genus (''[[Ipomoea]]'') of the bindweed family ([[Convolvulaceae]]). It is native to Mexico, El Salvador, Guatemala, and Honduras.<ref name=POWO>{{cite taxon |POWO |title=''Ipomoea pedicellaris'' Benth. |id=269491-1 |access-date=1 November 2025}}</ref>\n\n== References ==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q15485914}}\n\n[[Category:Ipomoea|pedicellaris]]\n[[Category:Plants described in 1845]]\n[[Category:Taxa named by George Bentham]]\n\n{{Solanales-stub}}",
